"new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINAGAWA TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAHARA, KEISUKE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NKK CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINAGAWA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUI SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAHARA KEISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINAGAWA TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAHARA, KEISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINAGAWA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Component regulating materials are added to incineration residue containing salts for regulation to within a component ratio range of 0.7 to 2.0 which is to be determined by (Ca + Mg)/(Si + Al). The component-ratio-regulated incineration residue is charged into a melting furnace kept in a reducing atmosphere to form molten substances which are separated into a molten slag layer, a molten salt layer and a molten metal layer. The molten slag is classified and discharged from the melting furnace for quenching after discharged. With a vapor phase portion in the melting furnace kept at 700 to 1000  DEG C, non-oxidizing gas is blown into the vapor phase portion to increase an exhaust gas amount from the melting furnace.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On ajoute des matériaux de régulation à des résidus d'incinération contenant des sels afin de les réguler dans une plage de rapports entre éléments de 0,7 à 2 devant être définie par (Ca + Mg)/(Si + Al). On charge ces résidus d'incinération, dont le rapport entre les différents éléments a été régulé, dans un four de fusion conservé sous atmosphère réductrice afin d'obtenir des substances en fusion qu'on sépare en une couche de scories en fusion, une couche de sels en fusion et une couche de métaux en fusion. On trie les scories en fusion et on les décharge du four de fusion afin d'en effectuer l'extinction. On introduit un gaz non oxydant dans une partie de phase vapeur du four de fusion conservé entre 700 et 1000  DEG C, de façon à augmenter la quantité de gaz d'échappement sortant du four de fusion.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>